{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/309176-angels-and-the-infrastructure-condition","id":309176,"title":"Angels and the Infrastructure condition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-11T09:01:04-08:00","id":309176,"title":"Angels and the Infrastructure condition","content":"I've got some questions about something I've never quite understood, the infrastructure condition. For the ephemeral entity rules I understand how ghosts and spirits work and are able to manifest but its less clear to me how angels do it. Some questions<br /> <br /> 1. Does an angel always have the infrastructure condition as long as the infrastructure is working or is it only on certain areas they have to remain in?<br /> <br /> 2. Given the angel has the infrastructure condition how does it change it in to the open condition? And what has to remain true for it to remain open? Do they use influences and does that mean they have to be near one of their influences to manifest and possibly remain near it while manifested?<br /> <br /> 3. Some of the angels in the GMC book are pretending to be people which seems like it means they are manifest almost all the time, so they'd be spending 3 essence about every hour I think. Is that right and if so are they just getting all kinds of essence somehow to keep that up or do they have a cover and the rules just didn't have that concept yet.<br /> <br /> 4. Obviously this one is not a cannon question, but how do you think angels generaly get essence/how much do they get? Do they have to worry about conserving it all or do they have as much as they could want?<br /> <br /> Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/92-ramza","name":"Ramza","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar92_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T16:04:57-08:00","id":309541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramza</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/309176-angels-and-the-infrastructure-condition#post309176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. Does an angel always have the infrastructure condition as long as the infrastructure is working or is it only on certain areas they have to remain in?</div> </div> </div> </div>infrastructure is infrastructure if it is on or not. It also doesn't have to remain in the infrastructure condition. I would think even infrastructure that is in disrepair would be fine for an angel as long as the linchpin is ok<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramza</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/309176-angels-and-the-infrastructure-condition#post309176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Given the angel has the infrastructure condition how does it change it in to the open condition? And what has to remain true for it to remain open? Do they use influences and does that mean they have to be near one of their influences to manifest and possibly remain near it while manifested?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah they need something that is similar to their influence. They can use numina to cause that though. For example an angel with the influence death can Implant a mission to someone to kill someone to summon. It is also why the God Machine uses cultist to bring angels to the world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramza</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/309176-angels-and-the-infrastructure-condition#post309176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. Some of the angels in the GMC book are pretending to be people which seems like it means they are manifest almost all the time, so they'd be spending 3 essence about every hour I think. Is that right and if so are they just getting all kinds of essence somehow to keep that up or do they have a cover and the rules just didn't have that concept yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>If a police department is infrastructure, then the people working there are part of the infrastructure. So an angel could hang out with police and be fine. There is a plot point in the GMC about people working at the place being elimination infrastructure without them knowing. Infrastructure is conceptual as it it can be physical. Cultist can also sacrifice things to give angels essence or steal it fro other beings if they have the right powers. People with the destiny merit also are infrastructure. People who have a destiny to die at a certain time to power infrastructure will have the infrastructure condition.<br /> <br /> It cost 3 essence to materialise and it last for one hour per success. It is a good question of how a angel says being materialised all day but think about this. An angels mission is to look after a kid so he does not die before his time. Materialise before he wakes up, feed him and send him to school. You could do that with one materialise roll, the most you need is 2 hours. Then the angel can follow the kid who is infrastructure of some kid in twilight, using numina or materialising when shit hits the fan as someone else. Now then angle mom &quot;get home from work&quot; at 8pm so then the angel only needs to materialise for a few hours. Okay the angel might lose some on parents evening or end up forced to spend a day out to the fun fair but there is a lot of time it can be powered down.<br /> <br /> But I myself would like to see what the writers had in mind for angels when it comes to covers, missions that involved at lot of hours saying materialised. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramza</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/309176-angels-and-the-infrastructure-condition#post309176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4. Obviously this one is not a cannon question, but how do you think angels generaly get essence/how much do they get? Do they have to worry about conserving it all or do they have as much as they could want?</div> </div> </div> </div>It matters for the plot. There is an infrastructure in one of the books that job is to give essence to angels in a certain radius. Does the God Machine drain insight from mortals in a think tank to use as angel batteries? Is that new serial killer a cultist feeding people to an angel? For occult physics to work it takes time, resources, things happening at certain places and certain times. This means it is up to the person running the game what exists in one city and what does in another. The infrastructure in the book thats job is to feed angels might only work in that location or the God Machine can only make one ever 74 years as the planets align a certain way.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4090-mental-state","name":"Mental-State","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T17:31:36-08:00","id":309659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramza</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/309176-angels-and-the-infrastructure-condition#post309176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Does an angel always have the infrastructure condition as long as the infrastructure is working or is it only on certain areas they have to remain in?</div> </div> </div> </div>Me and Satchel had an enlightening discussion about this half a year ago (you can find it <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/71851-unpacking-manifestation-conditions\">here</a>). We agreed that the system as presented in the book was unclear, but concluded that as the Infrastructure influence of Angels is differentiated (Angels have Influence Drugs, or Time for example), the infrastructure that supplies them with Essence should also be differentiated. So Angels only generate Essence in proximity of relevantly flavoured infrastructure.<br /> <br /> The book notes that anything that has been prepared by the God Machine in a certain way (often through extended action of cultists, unwitting pawns or other angels and probably also through occult matrices) counts a Infrastructure for the relevant angel. I must note that the mention of the Destiny Merit is left over from an earlier draft when there was still a Fate mechanic related to the God Machine, so you should ignore that.<br /> <br /> Technically, the Angel does not have to stay near its infrastructure, but it bleeds one Essence per hour while away. So angels still have to return frequently to not fall into hibernation. Angels that have to leave their infrastructure often without materializing or a target to fetter themselves to, probably need somekind of refueling infrastructure that provides a greater amount of Essence, or cultists that directly sacrifice to it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramza</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/309176-angels-and-the-infrastructure-condition#post309176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Given the angel has the infrastructure condition how does it change it in to the open condition? And what has to remain true for it to remain open? Do they use influences and does that mean they have to be near one of their influences to manifest and possibly remain near it while manifested?</div> </div> </div> </div>Like you say, to materialize, possess or become material in any other way, angels have to be near an Open Condition. The GMC book isn't entirely clear on how to create this condition. It can at be done by the angel itself (or its cultists) by fine tuning the Infrastructure condition in an extended action. Furthermore, the Angel can use either Strengthen Influence (according to the diagram) or Control Influence (according to the text). I hope this inconsistency will be fixed in the 2nd edition book.<br /> <br /> The Open condition remains as long as it is not disturbed enough. Normally it stays as long as the underlying Infrastructure keeps existing.<br /> <br /> If the Angel used Materialize in a location that is Open, he can leave this location afterwards without problems. He should try to return before Materialize runs out to avoid Essence bleed, but that is it. Another option would be preparing a person, or physical automaton by making it Open and fettering the Angel to it, or even Claiming it. This would allow even more freedom of movement (as long as the Angel stays in control) as the Angel wouldn't have to return to avoid Essence bleed. I would assume that Claiming prepared corpses, automatons or persons would be a good way for an Angel to operate for a long time in a low Essence environment.<br /> <br /> If the Open condition were to be removed while the Angel was still Materialized, he would be returned to Twilight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramza</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/309176-angels-and-the-infrastructure-condition#post309176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. Some of the angels in the GMC book are pretending to be people which seems like it means they are manifest almost all the time, so they'd be spending 3 essence about every hour I think. Is that right and if so are they just getting all kinds of essence somehow to keep that up or do they have a cover and the rules just didn't have that concept yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean to use the word Materialized instead of Manifest, as Manifestation is the whole category of ways to appear in the material world. Even Twilight Form is called a Manifestation. Also it is not three essence per hour, but for three Essence they can remain material for a number of hours equal to the number of successes on their Power + Finesse roll. But this will still cost a lot of essence.<br /> <br /> So the options I see here are access to some kind of refueling facilty that directly replenishes Essence, a cult that regularly sacrifices to the Angel, or the claiming of a mortal (or possibly corpse or automaton). I would guess that if an Angel had to pretend to be a person, a method would be provided to do this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramza</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/309176-angels-and-the-infrastructure-condition#post309176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4. Obviously this one is not a cannon question, but how do you think angels generaly get essence/how much do they get? Do they have to worry about conserving it all or do they have as much as they could want?</div> </div> </div> </div>I rule that the Essence they gain from staying near their relevant Infrastructure is free. God Machine infrastructure is just suffused by Essence, that the Angel would slowly absorb. All the extra Essence an Angel needs, has to come frome sacrifice, either directly to the Angel, or done somewhere else and transported to the Angel. So the amount of Essence of an Angel is limited by the amount of people the God Machine is willing to sacrifice to reach its goal, without also compromising other goals.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}